>> quaff your potion to get one level up. Switch to the assault rifle
>> before you go downstairs. You are now in a boulder fort with Demogorgon
>> two squares away from you. [...]

> Curious; why an uncursed scroll if all you want is block the stairs?

I do not want to just block the stairs. I want that he cannot touch
me... That's the whole point. I do not like the illness and stunning
attacks for which I may not have a 100% cure, with unicorn horns working
only at a lower percentage. Even if I have cure sickness at 0%, as long
as I am stunned, I cannot really fight back. (So I think converting one
of his illness attacks into a stunning one has not made him less
dangerous, rather the opposite. You may need two moves to heal in each
round, so he can get in another round of attacking you before you can
hit him. And he decreases your HP all the time, unless you quaff a
potion of invulnerability.) Of course, I could engrave Elbereth on the
stairs as well. (Probably not successfully while I am stunned.) But I
want to rely on it as rarely as possible. And I might scuff it out,
before I am really done with him. Being in a boulder fort, I can take my
time attacking him, as *he* cannot get at *me*. Also monsters that he
may summon will have a hard time getting at me. (If there are giants
among them, then this is not true anymore, but any giant I can kill
immediately after he has occupied a boulder square, will close the gap
he has opened.)

> Then one boulder (from cursed scroll) should suffice. If you use an
> uncursed one with the described procedure, Demogorgon will have 16
> squares space (to dance around the 9 boulders)

Most of the time he will not have all of them, because there are some
maze walls left or the stairs is near a corner or wall. Since he is
changing position frequently, it does not matter, if he sometimes is not
in a direct line for shooting at him. He will get back into line soon
enough. In any case, normally all you need is about two or three rounds
of 5 blessed +4 bullets.

> and only 8 of them
> will be reachable in a straight line from the stairs with missile
> weapons. If there's only one boulder on the stairs Demogorgon would
> dance around the eight adjacent squares which are all reachable by
> your missile weapons. (Or is Slashem here different from Vanilla?)

No. But I would have to rely on Elbereth all the time. And to use
missiles would be completely unnecessary... If I happen to scuff out the
writing, he may get in a few illness attacks (or more than a few, if he
stuns me, too). My approach is devised to keep that number down to zero.
Demogorgon is dangerous, if you allow him to get next to you and I want
to keep that danger to a minimum.


